{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "A Comedy of Errors", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Not Again!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 10, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Understand detailed descriptions of real or imaginary events and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Present Unreal Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The Present Unreal Conditional is used to talk about what you generally would do in imaginary situations. The result of the condition is unclear and impossible to predict with certainty.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The Present Unreal Conditional is also called the second Conditional.</br> You use the structure: </br><span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">If</span>... Simple Past, .... would</span>+<span class=\"italic\">verb </span></br><span class=\"italic\">or Would+verb ...<span class=\"strong\"> if </span>... Simple Past.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:  <span class=\"italic\">If I won the lottery, I would definitely travel the world.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The outcome is unclear, and it is impossible to know whether you will win the lottery in the future or not.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">If I were you, I would tell her that you are not into online dating.</span></br>You use<span class=\"italic\"> If I were you </span>... to give a strong piece of advice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " If I won the lottery, I would definitely travel the world writing ... and eating and drinking.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I would be in the hospital in a week if I dated someone like her. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If I weren't specific, I would have had so many losers contacting me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If I were you, I would tell her that you are just not into those sort of things. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " If I were you, I'd change your pictures.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expressing Absence of Necessity", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the negative forms of the modals <span class=\"italic\">need to </span>and <span class=\"italic\">have to </span>to express absence of necessity in the past or in the present.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Absence of necessity is expressed with the<span class=\"strong\"> negative form of have to</span>, not with mustn't.</br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">You don't have to date her if you don't like her.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Absence of necessity can also be expressed by negative form of <span class=\"italic\">need</span>. It is generally used as a main verb in the construction <span class=\"italic\">don't need to</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You don't need to stay in contact with her.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You don't have to be picky.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You don't have to date her.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I don't need someone like this. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You don't need to date people you don't like.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "psycho", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a crazy or unstable person", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The killer was a psycho.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when you meet people online. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "aggressive", "type": "name"}, {"content": " boldly assertive and forward", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He is a very aggressive soccer player.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take a peek", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look; to glance quickly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"co